     "nota": "",
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "«De» also merges with them.",
     "texto": [
      "de + este = **deste**, de + esta = **desta**, de + esse = **desse**, de + aquele = **daquele**.",
      "As «gostar» takes «de», you will hear it all the time: **Gosto deste vestido** (I like this dress), **gosto desta camisa** (I like this shirt)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Clothes",
     "texto": [
      "**A roupa** is «clothes». **A camisa**, **o vestido**, **os sapatos**, **o casaco** (jacket or coat), **a saia** (skirt), **o chapéu** (hat).",
      "Trousers are **as calças**, always in the plural. Trainers are **as sapatilhas**.",
      "A trap: in Portugal **a camisola** is «the jumper».",
      "To say that something is nice or cute, the Portuguese say **giro / gira**. **Olha!** = look!"
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    }
   ]
  },
